# EAS Build uploads the whole monorepo root so pnpm can resolve workspace
# packages, but it does NOT respect nested per-package .gitignore files
# (only the root .gitignore). Build caches like apps/web/.next slip through
# and bloat the archive even though they're already properly gitignored
# and completely irrelevant to building the native app. Listed explicitly
# here so they're excluded regardless of what's locally present.

**/.next/
**/.turbo/
**/.vercel/
**/.wrangler/
**/.output/
**/.nitro/
**/dist/
**/build/
**/coverage/
**/*.log
**/.DS_Store

# Native projects are meant to be CNG-managed (generated fresh from
# app.config.js by EAS Build's own prebuild step), not hand-committed.
# If a stray apps/native/android or apps/native/ios ever reappears locally
# (e.g. from running `expo prebuild` without --clean), EAS Build silently
# detects it and uses whatever's hardcoded there instead of app.config.js —
# which is exactly what caused the .dev app-variant package suffix to be
# ignored. Excluded here so that can never happen again.
apps/native/android/
apps/native/ios/
